Outside a git repository a `.gitignore` doesn't apply: the parent's `*.md` rule doesn't hide `pkg/a.md` from the glob view.
== args
input/pkg
== file input/.gitignore
*.md
== file input/pkg/a.md
---
description: Parent .gitignore does not apply outside a git repo.
---
# a
== stdout
glob view: input/pkg
input/pkg/a.md (4 lines): description: "Parent .gitignore does not apply outside a git repo."
== stderr
== exit 0
